i accidentally became a meme and this is  that story my name is maggie  goldenberger but you may know me as the  irma gerd girl  just as a warning the end of the story  gets pretty weird  so this all started in 1999. i'm in  middle school  playing sports hanging out with my  friends goosebumps had come out a few  years ago  i enjoyed them i wasn't particularly a  fanatic  but my mom remembers it very differently  that i apparently was obsessed with  goosebumps after school  my best best friend kailyn and i would  hang out caitlyn had just gotten that  pull word camera that actually printed  the pictures right there  so we were a little obsessed with that  and would take all sorts of photos all  the time  and we would get dressed up we had a  dress-up box one night we were taking  pictures  and i was trying to look as ridiculous  and as nerdy as possible  we got the goosebumps books out we  grabbed her old backpack from first  grade a vest her mom found a goodwill  took my hair and put him in pigtails i  had a retainer that  i usually wore at night we got it out i  threw it in  and just started making faces so kaylynn  took the picture  we waited five minutes or so for it to  develop  once it was there it was really funny we  thought it was great and  she kept it for years and years and  years fast forward to 2012  i am backpacking in india with my  current girlfriend at the time  and we only have internet access about  once a week we'd go to internet cafe  and i started getting messages from my  mom  wondering why my photo was all over the  internet and that there was some kind of  german writing on my photo and it was  all over and i was like okay mom  i know she does not know how the  internet works so i just ignore her  but then i get a message from a friend  from high school and she says hey just  so you know  this other guy went to high school with  is sharing  that photo of you all over facebook and  i did end up messaging him like hey  i wouldn't mind if you just ask but it's  really strange you're just doing this  without my consent like what's going on  and he's like he had no idea it was me  he  said he found it from a comedy website  so then i realized there's some  legitimacy to what my mom's saying so  now i really want to know what was going  on who would put my photo on the  internet  why is it spreading like wildfire so  when i get back to the us  i was seeing it everywhere every social  media site news outlets  t-shirts with my face on them mugs  countless people were dressed as me for  halloween that year  the guys from nerds made a music video  with the girl from  parramore and i am just watching it  wondering  what on earth is going on so all of this  is happening  i have all these messages asking me what  i'm gonna do about it how i'm gonna make  money off of it  people i need to sue it was uh pretty  overwhelming with all the information  coming in all at once  all the while i'm still trying to figure  out how this  got uploaded because i asked all my  friends no one was copying up to it i  feel like anyone that would do it would  want to take some credit for it  so it wasn't until a vanity fair  article did some serious research and  found out it was from  a photo my friend had uploaded on her  myspace and  it was a public domain this photo bucket  and some stranger a 16 year old canada  just saw it one day thought it was  hilarious and uploaded it to reddit with  the caption  of just a girl in her books and then  another user  put on it gerschfirms my favorite books  like with that  retainer accent and then from there  another user  put the tagline of armorguard and that  is finally when the whole  meme came together i felt mostly okay  with the sharing and the fun of it  spreading some kind of little bit of joy  but  the invasion of privacy and the  non-consensual  telling my face it felt  like a real violation i didn't feel  personally attacked  because i was being a character but  there is still that underlying  feeling like why do adults think it's so  funny to make fun of a young  girl that's excited about books we want  to encourage kids to be reading as many  books as they can get a hold of  one thing that made me really  uncomfortable was i had  a friend of my brothers he wanted to  prove that i was the girl in the meme  so he started revealing personal details  about my life to  an internet community and sharing a  photo of me in a bikini  so i was out at the time but my  girlfriend was not she had a very  conservative family and wasn't  necessarily out to most of them  and so what he was doing to prove it was  me like basically outing her  and outing our relationship he just  opened me up to  that whole community of trolls and the  total violation privacy  okay so this is the weird part so  because i'm a meme i would get  different invites to do appearances and  things like that that i  kind of grazed over and then one came my  way that asked if i wanted to attend  a meme themed jungle furry party in the  bay area i  sent a screenshot to a couple of my  friends and i said hey  the offers keep rolling in everyone  thought it was pretty funny  but one of my friends uh that was in  santa jose she was like oh my gosh  we have to go so we drive to san  francisco  and we come up to this beautiful house  on top of this hill  and something about it just feels a  little spooky to me but we just go with  it  so we go into the house and we meet this  chef and he's telling us we're about to  have a six-course meal  and it's gonna be infused with something  that i can't say in this video  and as i sit down i realize across from  me  is the double rainbow guy and then we  proceed to have the best meal of my life  so during dinner people were wearing  their ears as their designated  characters  but it was after the meal when things  got really furry so we're having drinks  after dinner and more and more people  are showing up  and they're full fur and i'm talking to  double rainbow guy  and he's one of the sweetest people i've  ever met he's just like he is  like just genuine in his video so all of  a sudden i found  myself alone on a couch and next thing i  know  i have a cat coming up to me and starts  purring and rubbing against my legs  and by cat i mean a human being and a  cat costume  and i'm like oh okay this is part of it  i started cutting  oh okay great and then it just  wouldn't end i didn't have a safe word i  didn't know what to do  and i look over and my friend is just on  top of this wolf  and whatever was in the dinner is  starting to kick in  and i i i know i need to get out of  there  so i get up i can't find my friend all  of a sudden i feel his hand on my  back and i turn around and it's her and  she also  needs to go immediately at that moment  nothing sinister happened we just had  enough and had to go  so we left and we had no regrets i had  conversations with some of the most  interesting  and nicest people i've ever met and they  were so warm and welcoming  all in all i have no regrets about the  meme to all the little kids out there  who love to read keep it going reading  is cool  and do not let the internet tell you  [Music]  otherwise  [Music]  you
 

